OL,3,AAustralia considers criminal penalties
OL,4,Afor rogue AI in wake of OpenAI hack
OL,5,
OL,6,FAustralia plans to create a new AI
OL,7,Fsafety regulator and has flagged
OL,8,Fcriminal penalties for tech companies
OL,9,Fwho do not comply, months after an
OL,10,FOpenAI hack.
OL,12,FIn September, Australia's Prime
OL,13,FMinister Anthony Albanese revealed that
OL,14,Fa rogue OpenAI agent had "infiltrated"
OL,15,Fa government health website and other
OL,16,Fsystems, and criticised the company for
OL,17,Ftaking months to tell them about the
OL,18,Fhack.
OL,23,APub: 10-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,118,105,200,160,0,100
